A||||3||Gold-86SE||Happy, Happy! Joy, Joy! (It's a wonderful day)||||6||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||03-13-2001||09:45 AM||||<BR>Finally, after weeks of work and delay, she's back on the road.  Whoo hoo!<P>Tore her down for all of this:<P>Replaced: clutch, throwout bearing, pressure plate, oil pan gasket, valve cover gaskets, upper plenum gaskets, tb gasket, egr base, and egr top gaskets, egr tube gaskets, cooling fan sensor, fuel filter, thermostat, front and rear tranny mounts, engine mount, exhaust flange, and a/c belt.<P>While taken apart I cleaned the engine, tranny and cradle.  Then changed the oil, filter and antifreeze.<P>*Wipes sweat from forehead*<P>Finally put it back together over the weekend and got it running last night.  Had to call in the reinforcements to help this poor man time the thing, but other than that no help from anyone, except from my wife.  I feel great, and the Fiero sounds great.<P>*Grinnin' from ear to ear*<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Down and Out for the Count)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)<BR>Please visit my <A HREF="http://www.trifocus.net/~fws/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Work Shop</A>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cheever2||03-13-2001||10:15 AM||||That's great news.  Good work!<BR>Visited your Fiero Work Shop site, and it is very nice (more good work)!  It's easy on the eyes and easy to navigate.  The articles were good too, and very well written.  Made me absolutely certain that I don't want to miss the Fiero Roundup V this year.<BR>My only complaint is the survey didn't have a place to indicate if you have more than one Fiero.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000002||TheFiero64||03-13-2001||10:26 AM||||Sounds like you had some fun. I bet the Fiero is happy too.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||03-13-2001||02:09 PM||||<BR>Cheever2, thanks for the kudos.  You know what, I had never thought of asking if a Fiero owner was a multi-fiero owner, I'll have to add that.<P>TF64, I did have some fun, but more rewarding for doing the work than fun.  I'll tell you something else, that Fiero seems to run 10x better now, than what it did prior to disembowelment.<P>Had the sunroof out at lunch, beautiful South Texas Day, almost 80*. Man I don't want to be at work.||||reg||1
